{"frame":"event","cursor":87,"box":"nothing-to-do/w1-m20261127050616","box_id":3,"session":3,"kind":"steered","payload":{"inbox":3,"session":"moor-3","message":"Each run applies the work list in WORKLIST.md at the repo root, one commit per item, and opens one pull request for them. moor holds the run open until its gates pass, in order: gate `applied`, evidence `applied.md` listing each item with its commit; then gate `pull-request`, evidence `pr.md` holding the pull request URL, with a check that the pull request is open. When WORKLIST.md is missing or lists nothing, the run ends with the outcome `nothing to do` (plain), which can end a run before its gates pass.\n\nmoor keeps this Box open until its gates pass. The gates open in this order, one at a time, and the Box is done only when all have passed. The first gate is in hand now.\n\n- Gate `applied`: leave applied.md in .moor/artifacts/, then call report_step with step \"applied\", result ok, those names and a one-line note of what you did. moor runs its check itself once you are quiet. It looks for: “applied.md lists at least one commit and every commit it names exists in the repo.”.\n- Gate `pull-request`: leave pr.md in .moor/artifacts/, then call report_step with step \"pull-request\", result ok, those names and a one-line note of what you did. moor runs its check itself once you are quiet. It looks for: “pr.md holds a pull request URL and that pull request is open.”.\n\nThe run's outcomes, in the order moor tries them: the first whose checks all pass is how the run ends. moor tries them once every gate has passed, and tries those marked \"anytime\" also whenever you stop before the gate in hand has passed.\n\n- `nothing to do`: WORKLIST.md is missing or lists no items, so there was nothing to apply. (anytime) It holds when: “WORKLIST.md is missing or has no list items.”\n- `pull request opened`: The work list was applied and one pull request was opened for it.","submit_retried":false,"turn_before":0},"ts":1